WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.770
Energy is a practical resource that affects attention, quality, judgment, consistency, learning, and relationships.

2
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.199
It is not the same as time, motivation, or discipline.

3
00:00:11.199 --> 00:00:21.864
Open calendar space may still lack usable capacity if attention is fragmented, emotional energy is depleted, cognitive load is high, or recovery has been neglected.

4
00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:25.292
Better planning begins by seeing capacity honestly.

5
00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:28.644
Strong energy management matches work to capacity.

6
00:00:28.644 --> 00:00:40.757
It uses high-energy windows for demanding work, batches shallow work where possible, reduces context switching, and designs routines that make important work easier to start and finish.

7
00:00:40.757 --> 00:00:50.812
It also reduces avoidable drains such as unclear priorities, open loops, excessive meetings, hidden emotional labor, constant availability, and rework.

8
00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:53.631
Recovery is not separate from performance.

9
00:00:53.631 --> 00:00:58.354
It is one of the conditions that makes sustainable performance possible.

10
00:00:58.354 --> 00:01:08.791
Breaks, transitions, movement, broad attention to basic needs, emotional decompression, and adequate non-work time all help preserve attention and judgment.

11
00:01:08.791 --> 00:01:17.628
This course stays non-clinical, but it is practical to recognize that people produce better work when they are not treated like machines.

12
00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:20.218
The goal is not constant high intensity.

13
00:01:20.218 --> 00:01:27.989
The goal is reliable performance through better pacing, clearer priorities, recovery, and realistic workload design.

14
00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:34.235
At the team level, this means respecting shared capacity and reducing reliance on heroic effort.

15
00:01:34.235 --> 00:01:45.129
At the individual level, it means using energy deliberately, noticing patterns, and building systems that support real life rather than pretending limits do not exist.
